{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00127",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.26,
      "end_seconds": 6.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "Doctor, this one's ready for you. Everything's on the chart, but I'll go through it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.89,
      "end_seconds": 11.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Thank you. Good morning, tell me what's been going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.83,
      "end_seconds": 25.75,
      "duration_seconds": 12.92,
      "text": "Honestly, it's trouble sleeping, and my family pushed me to come. It's the not knowing that gets to me. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.3,
      "end_seconds": 28.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.25,
      "end_seconds": 34.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "For nearly five years, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.08,
      "end_seconds": 40.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.47,
      "end_seconds": 53.94,
      "duration_seconds": 12.47,
      "text": "It settles a little with a warm bath. Pretty moderate, if I'm being honest. Yes, screens at night. That makes it worse. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.94,
      "end_seconds": 57.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.39,
      "end_seconds": 60.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "It usually comes with trouble concentrating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.49,
      "end_seconds": 66.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 66.96,
      "end_seconds": 72.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.9,
      "end_seconds": 75.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.39,
      "end_seconds": 84.11,
      "duration_seconds": 7.72,
      "text": "The trouble concentrating? That's been for two years. Uh, I've also been feeling irritable, for two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.52,
      "end_seconds": 88.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Have you had trouble sleeping before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.24,
      "end_seconds": 94.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened last year, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 98.94,
      "end_seconds": 101.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Mm, that's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.56,
      "end_seconds": 106.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Have you had any night sweats, heavy caffeine or snoring?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.59,
      "end_seconds": 117.77,
      "duration_seconds": 10.18,
      "text": "No, no night sweats, no heavy caffeine, no snoring. I was feeling exhausted in the day at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.88,
      "end_seconds": 121.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Any restless legs, chest pain or low mood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.05,
      "end_seconds": 128.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "I haven't had restless legs, chest pain or low mood, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.54,
      "end_seconds": 131.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.76,
      "end_seconds": 135.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "I mean, you know, no, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 137.32,
      "end_seconds": 146.17,
      "duration_seconds": 8.85,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Respiratory rate 14, pulse 65, pressure 124 over 70, temperature is 37.0 degrees, SpO2 98 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.98,
      "end_seconds": 151.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Alright, good, thank you. Do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.2,
      "end_seconds": 159.23,
      "duration_seconds": 7.03,
      "text": "Oh, you know, yes, penicillin, it gives me hives. I'm allergic to eggs, I get stomach cramps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.61,
      "end_seconds": 163.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.63,
      "end_seconds": 169.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "My father had a heart attack. My uncle had colon cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.49,
      "end_seconds": 174.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.21,
      "end_seconds": 180.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "So, um, I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.08,
      "end_seconds": 185.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Okay, any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.34,
      "end_seconds": 193.47,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "Sodium valproate. I take it 500 milligrams, maybe, twice a day for the fits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.8,
      "end_seconds": 197.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.19,
      "end_seconds": 201.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.02,
      "end_seconds": 209.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a small white one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.34,
      "end_seconds": 212.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.7,
      "end_seconds": 226.16,
      "duration_seconds": 12.46,
      "text": "For my heart, I believe. My daughter sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Yeah, I'd been on clopidogrel, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.61,
      "end_seconds": 228.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.06,
      "end_seconds": 236.06,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "Right, uh, just a bypass operation, six years ago. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.33,
      "end_seconds": 242.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "Any long-term health problems I should know about? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.03,
      "end_seconds": 251.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.51,
      "text": "So, I've had anxiety for about ten years now. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.1,
      "end_seconds": 254.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.07,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.77,
      "end_seconds": 265.47,
      "duration_seconds": 9.7,
      "text": "Uh, yes, high blood pressure. I just want to get back to normal, really. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.82,
      "end_seconds": 266.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.2,
      "end_seconds": 283.76,
      "duration_seconds": 16.56,
      "text": "Epilepsy, for nearly five years. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. My family kept telling me to get it checked. I have heart disease. I took the morning off to come in today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.71,
      "end_seconds": 288.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Is there anything you were hoping to get out of today's visit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.94,
      "end_seconds": 296.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Mostly I just want to understand what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.23,
      "end_seconds": 302.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.08,
      "end_seconds": 312.93,
      "duration_seconds": 9.85,
      "text": "Yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.32,
      "end_seconds": 341.22,
      "duration_seconds": 27.9,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. My working impression is insomnia, probably stress-related. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. It could also be sleep apnoea, so we'll keep that open. I can't rule out a thyroid problem yet. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had trouble sleeping for nearly five years, moderate, and no restless legs or low mood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.02,
      "end_seconds": 344.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Oh, exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.2,
      "end_seconds": 350.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.76,
      "end_seconds": 353.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "It's perfect, you know, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.13,
      "end_seconds": 360.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.17,
      "text": "Let's get a sleep study, for insomnia. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 360.69,
      "end_seconds": 364.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "We have a slot Friday at 3:30 pm, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.18,
      "end_seconds": 366.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Okay, I'll be there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.61,
      "end_seconds": 374.7,
      "duration_seconds": 7.09,
      "text": "We should do a thyroid test for insomnia. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 375.41,
      "end_seconds": 376.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.01,
      "end_seconds": 403.12,
      "duration_seconds": 26.11,
      "text": "Same wake-up time every day, no screens in the hour before bed, and no coffee after lunch. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 404.51,
      "end_seconds": 405.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.87,
      "end_seconds": 412.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "Please don't sit on it if the symptoms get worse. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 413.04,
      "end_seconds": 414.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 415.35,
      "end_seconds": 418.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Please come and see me in four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 419.08,
      "end_seconds": 419.78,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 422.72,
      "end_seconds": 428.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "Let me check that I've been clear. What will you do once you get home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 429.35,
      "end_seconds": 434.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "So, uh, I come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 434.89,
      "end_seconds": 437.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Good. Look after yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 438.16,
      "end_seconds": 442.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "Okay, you know, so thank you. I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 443.46,
      "end_seconds": 444.33,
      "duration_seconds": 0.87,
      "text": "Alright, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}